{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking","id":892837,"title":"[2e] Dream Form vs. dreamwalking?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-17T15:44:44-07:00","id":892837,"title":"[2e] Dream Form vs. dreamwalking?","content":"The dreamwalking system in Changeling's second edition makes no reference at all to the rules for Dream Forms that appear in Beast and Mage 2e. That prompts the question - are characters currently in a Dream Form, projecting their minds outside their bodies, valid targets for a changeling's dreamwalking powers? Do they, that is, form bastions in the Hedge that changelings and other Hedge creatures can meddle with?<br /> <br /> If I followed my own inclinations I would say No - astral travel may look like sleep from the outside, but it's really just as much a conscious state as normal waking is. The astral traveler is not dreaming, he's mentally absent. But I'm not writing for Changeling, Beast or Mage, so if there's an official answer ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T16:15:02-07:00","id":892860,"title":"","content":"I don't write for any of those, but the way I see Dream Bastions in the Hedge, they basicly pools of dream glamour that form pocket planes in the Hedge.<br /> <br /> So the Changeling who enters one is still in the Hedge, but as long as the Dream is going, the Dream Bastion conforms to it the Dream, unless some alters the Dream Bastion, which in turn alters that Dream.<br /> <br /> When the Too Solid Tilt happens, the connect between the Dream and the Dream Bastion is strenthen, embedding some Goetia into the Glamour that makes up the Dream Bastion. <br /> <br /> The parts of the Dream Bastion that get the most Goetia, &quot;become real&quot;, like Incubi.<br /> <br /> If a dream gets pulled into the Beasts lair and a Fay is in it, then that Fay plays by the Beasts rules.<br /> <br /> If a Beasts/Horror ends up stuck in the Hedge and enters a Dream Bastion, it plays by Changeling rules.<br /> <br /> Just my Hypothesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T18:48:10-07:00","id":892925,"title":"","content":"Since we only have teaser up until now I can't really give a solid reply (beyond what omega above stated).<br /> <br /> For concrete rulings we'll have to wait for the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T18:59:26-07:00","id":892936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking#post892837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dreamwalking system in Changeling's second edition makes no reference at all to the rules for Dream Forms that appear in Beast and Mage 2e. That prompts the question - are characters currently in a Dream Form, projecting their minds outside their bodies, valid targets for a changeling's dreamwalking powers? Do they, that is, form bastions in the Hedge that changelings and other Hedge creatures can meddle with?<br /> <br /> If I followed my own inclinations I would say No - astral travel may look like sleep from the outside, but it's really just as much a conscious state as normal waking is. The astral traveler is not dreaming, he's mentally absent. But I'm not writing for Changeling, Beast or Mage, so if there's an official answer ...</div> </div> </div> </div>So, let's chat.<br /> <br /> As it stands now, Changelings predominately enter dreams physically at all times. In their own sleep, in the mortal world at least, they have the choice of the Gate of Horn or the Gate of Ivory, which basically is the choice of slipping into the dream world and receiving the benefits of sleep, or staying in the mortal world but not regaining Willpower. In the Hedge, they form a Bastion when they sleep.<br /> <br /> So, basically, every time a Changeling is in a dream, they are there in full. Their flesh and blood is dream and stories, and as such they don't just dip into the Skein-they dive head first and swim deep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T19:45:44-07:00","id":892955,"title":"","content":"The thing is, we have no rules currently what beings other than Changelings do inside dreams from just that preview. We can extrapolate from Mage and Beast if someone owns those books. Are we meant to use those rules for non-changelings or does everyone use their normal attributes, etc? Do non-changelings add their supernatural advantage to derived traits?<br /> <br /> &quot;Dream Health&quot; and &quot;Soul Shock&quot; in particular doesn't mesh well with Changeling. In Changeling, a non-lucid dreamer only doesn't recover willpower when &quot;killed&quot; in a dream. A lucid dreamer has their damage downgraded. In Mage and Beast any dreamer who &quot;does&quot; in a dream just suffers Soul Shock unless they are physically present (i.e. a Beast's Horror).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 05-17-2016, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T20:06:56-07:00","id":892969,"title":"","content":"Incubi use the Dream Form rules. True Fae and Huntsment operate on changeling principles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T22:57:44-07:00","id":893053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking#post892837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I followed my own inclinations I would say No - astral travel may look like sleep from the outside, but it's really just as much a conscious state as normal waking is. The astral traveler is not dreaming, he's mentally absent. But I'm not writing for Changeling, Beast or Mage, so if there's an official answer ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you're correct here. In spite of the term 'dream form' and 'oneiros' being hijacked by mage to mean the soul, dreams are not the realm of the soul. Mages and Beasts do all of their shenanigans in the oneiros not in <i>actual</i> dreams. There's some definite linguistic confusion going on though that irritates me. I would treat mages and beasts as normal, mundane dreamers with no special dream related powers unless they have something that specifically affects dreams and not the oneiros. Magic can still be used IN dreams, but they're not automatically lucid dreamers either. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T00:25:23-07:00","id":893097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=893053#post893053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that you're correct here. In spite of the term 'dream form' and <b>'oneiros' being hijacked by mage</b> to mean the soul</div> </div> </div> </div>My friend I have some extremely bad news for you from the far-off era of 2005.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T07:27:55-07:00","id":893287,"title":"","content":"The Greeks might have some input on the subject, and was what I was referring to. &quot;Oneiro-&quot; literally means &quot;Dream&quot; in Greek. So making it mean something completely different? It's very illogical and unintuitive. You'd ASSUME it means actual Dreams and many people obviously do. They'd have been better off using some word indicating the soul or spirit (real world spirit, not in game spirits) and then there wouldn't be a lingering illogical linguistic artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T07:55:43-07:00","id":893303,"title":"","content":".... to be honest, Temenos makes more sense for the name of the thing that currently has the name of Oneiros going by the actual meanings of the words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T09:05:48-07:00","id":893363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=892936#post892936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it stands now, Changelings predominately enter dreams physically at all times. In their own sleep, in the mortal world at least, they have the choice of the Gate of Horn or the Gate of Ivory, which basically is the choice of slipping into the dream world and receiving the benefits of sleep, or staying in the mortal world but not regaining Willpower. In the Hedge, they form a Bastion when they sleep.<br /> <br /> So, basically, every time a Changeling is in a dream, they are there in full. Their flesh and blood is dream and stories, and as such they don't just dip into the Skein-they dive head first and swim deep.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=892969#post892969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incubi use the Dream Form rules. True Fae and Huntsment operate on changeling principles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the information ... but it doesn't have much to do with the question. I'm asking if characters who are capable of Astral travel count as dreaming under changeling principles while they're in the Astral. It's the sort of thing that would come up in a Mage/Changeling crossover: If, say, a changeling found a mage entranced in his demesne, and tried dreamriding or dreamscaping on him, what would happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T09:07:40-07:00","id":893365,"title":"","content":"Good question. I legitimately don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T09:10:38-07:00","id":893367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=893287#post893287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Greeks might have some input on the subject, and was what I was referring to. &quot;Oneiro-&quot; literally means &quot;Dream&quot; in Greek. So making it mean something completely different? It's very illogical and unintuitive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes, the completely different space inside your soul where most sub-worlds by quantity seemingly only exist when someone's observing them, where your mental baggage is processed by repeating scenes, where metaphorical solutions to metaphorical problems can have real effects on your mentality, and where the whole collection of parts is the first proper level of a continuum of realms that include the home of beings whose primary impact on humanity is through nightmares and the subsection of the world-soul that is called <i>the Dreamtime</i> or <i>the Dreaming Earth</i> depending on who you ask.<br /> <br /> Have you actually read the relevant bits of Mage? At all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=893303#post893303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... to be honest, Temenos makes more sense for the name of the thing that currently has the name of Oneiros going by the actual meanings of the words.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no, seeing as &quot;place where you can talk to the gods/'gods' human culture worships&quot; is about as near to a sacred enclosure as one gets without dipping into the realms of things that wear those masks on top of more predatory or alien identities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:47:17-07:00","id":893629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=893367#post893367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, no, seeing as &quot;place where you can talk to the gods/'gods' human culture worships&quot; is about as near to a sacred enclosure as one gets without dipping into the realms of things that wear those masks on top of more predatory or alien identities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except a Temenos doesn't have All the gods in it. It is the divine place of a god. It makes no sense for it to be the place of all human culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T15:30:49-07:00","id":893667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=893629#post893629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except a Temenos doesn't have All the gods in it. It is the divine place of a god. It makes no sense for it to be the place of all human culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I invite you to examine the root word of &quot;culture.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T15:55:42-07:00","id":893689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=892936#post892936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, let's chat.<br /> <br /> As it stands now, Changelings predominately enter dreams physically at all times. In their own sleep, in the mortal world at least, they have the choice of the Gate of Horn or the Gate of Ivory, which basically is the choice of slipping into the dream world and receiving the benefits of sleep, or staying in the mortal world but not regaining Willpower. In the Hedge, they form a Bastion when they sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of the few things about 2E that I haven't liked so far. The inability to gain the benefits of sleep without disappearing seems like a pretty huge hole in their ability to remain hidden. In my games, I'm going to add a third option. The Gate of Horn shall still allow the full body lucid dreaming effect, while the Gate of Ivory will allow them to dream as a mortal does, but leaves them as vulnerable as anyone else to dream meddling. They will get the ability to turn off their dreams entirely by refusing to go through either gate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T19:42:31-07:00","id":893811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=893667#post893667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I invite you to examine the root word of &quot;culture.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That statement has no impact on what I said at all. I mean, they have the same root word as word for growing plants and farming, are you suggesting that all the plant souls should be in the Temenos just because the word Cultivate exists? No of course you aren't.<br /> <br /> Please go off the actual meanings of the words rather than trying to distract though trivia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T20:00:22-07:00","id":893822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=893811#post893811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please go off the actual meanings of the words rather than trying to distract though trivia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pointing out that the word for culture and the word &quot;cult&quot; come from the same root is &quot;trying to distract through trivia.&quot;<br /> <br /> Despite there being <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters\">an entire game</a> that plays with the connection between these things in the Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Despite &quot;gods&quot; as they relate to humanity being notoriously centrally influential on human culture.<br /> <br /> Despite Temenotic goetia being as near as one gets to an accessible audience with the gods of human culture without running afoul of either the periphery hazards of dealing with the ineffable or the material consequences of attributing humanlike concepts of divinity to what are essentially extremely smart wild animals or unusually lucid pseudoconscious aliens.<br /> <br /> I see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T01:59:47-07:00","id":893909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=893822#post893822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pointing out that the word for culture and the word &quot;cult&quot; come from the same root is &quot;trying to distract through trivia.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well considering it also applies to words like Cultivate.... yes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite there being <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters\">an entire game</a> that plays with the connection between these things in the Chronicles of Darkness. </div> </div> </div>Has no impact on what I said... so yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite &quot;gods&quot; as they relate to humanity being notoriously centrally influential on human culture. </div> </div> </div>Not really. It is a big influence, but central is a gigantic stretch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite Temenotic goetia being as near as one gets to an accessible audience with the gods of human culture without running afoul of either the periphery hazards of dealing with the ineffable or the material consequences of attributing humanlike concepts of divinity to what are essentially extremely smart wild animals or unusually lucid pseudoconscious aliens. </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, because Pluto the dog, Lord Bowler, Bill Shorten, and Jonathan creek are all gods.... But whatever. Doesn't change that that the CoD temenos is Everything from human culture, while real meaning of Temenos is a specific Cut Off piece of land that is associated with a figure. If instead of the Temenos being one big thing it was many different isolated cut off realms like how each Onerios is it's own self-contained thing, it'd make sense.<br /> <br /> A Temenos is &quot;<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">is a piece of land cut off and assigned as an official domain&quot; but in CoD it for some reason &quot;is a thousand domains all mashed together in one piece of land&quot;.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T16:58:41-07:00","id":894426,"title":"","content":"I personally think they should have included the Dream Form rules and said they apply to non-Fae, and that changelings go in physically but use those systems for damaging others (i.e no damage downgraded; they cause soul shock when they kill someone non-physically, like everyone else). Whether Astral Travel counts as the same layer as the Skein doesn't matter, because Mages and Beasts use the Dream Form rules in actual dreams too (mage specifically explicitly says so in the dream travel spell). So, as it is, the mechanics simply don't mesh, and I really hope that's fixed in the final version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T20:47:19-07:00","id":894538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=893909#post893909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well considering it also applies to words like Cultivate.... yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>The modern sense of the word <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Culture#Etymology\" target=\"_blank\"><i>is derived from &quot;cultivate.</i><i>&quot;</i></a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not really. It is a big influence, but central is a gigantic stretch. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say &quot;central.&quot; I said &quot;centrally.&quot; I can say I live in Central Ohio without that being a claim that I am at the center of my state. Gods and other figures of major cultural resonance tend to occupy one of the most influential roles in the societies they're attached to, and it doesn't really matter if they're <i>the most</i> influential overall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah yes, because Pluto the dog, Lord Bowler, Bill Shorten, and Jonathan creek are all gods.... </div> </div> </div>Famous things sufficiently resonant to have a lasting place in the Temenos <i>are cultural icons</i>, and that's a category that happens to include most every god that multiple people know about. This is a very poor application of basic sarcasm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If instead of the Temenos being one big thing it was many different isolated cut off realms like how each Onerios is it's own self-contained thing, it'd make sense. </div> </div> </div>Do you know how the Temenos works at all? Even realms with thematic relation to each other aren't just geographically adjacent to their neighbors. This is a domain where you have to engage in narrative to get anywhere other than where you already are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Temenos is &quot;<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">is a piece of land cut off and assigned as an official domain&quot; but in CoD it for some reason &quot;is a thousand domains all mashed together in one piece of land&quot;.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside that mischaracterization of the geography of the unconscious, the classical Mediterranean, modern religious English, and Jungian senses all have more to say on it than &quot;we set this land aside for a thing&quot;; the first two use the term as a place where one worships the gods and/or where the gods dwell, and the third is \u2014 shocking, I know \u2014 a mental space where one can safely truck with the collective archetypes of the human unconscious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T22:34:06-07:00","id":894567,"title":"","content":"Milo? Satchel? I started this thread to discuss how the Beast/Mage 2e rules for Dream Forms work with the previewed dreamwalking subsystem in Changeling 2e. Whether the jargon Mage invented for parts of the Astral Realms was appropriately chosen not only has nothing to do with that topic, it's long since past mending. Would you mind taking that argument elsewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T23:17:40-07:00","id":894576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=894567#post894567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Milo? Satchel? I started this thread to discuss how the Beast/Mage 2e rules for Dream Forms work with the previewed dreamwalking subsystem in Changeling 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you've gotten discussion. There's not much further for it to go, seeing as nomenclatural confusion doesn't change the fact that the Astral is essentially another dimension that you pass through dreams to get to in the most commonplace method and 2e oneiromancy explicitly doesn't allow supernatural powers to genuinely draw on other parts of the cosmology and their denizens.<br /> <br /> The Hedge manifests Dream Bastions as a consequence of dreams happening and characters within a Dream Bastion react to damage differently to characters in a position to have a Dream Form outside drastic changes of venue like a hungry Horror dragging people's souls into its Lair. The fae interface contextualizes the interaction in a manner that uses the fae mechanics; any encounters with Dream Form characters that a changeling is liable to run into (short of stumbling across a mage in their own dreams) is generally going to be an intruder using a supernatural trick different from the ones changelings and other fae use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T01:09:51-07:00","id":894609,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Stop the semantics argument. Thank you.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T06:02:21-07:00","id":894680,"title":"","content":"I think the answer to how the two systems interact would be a good question for The Hedge supplement or the Beast Players Guide to answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T08:34:08-07:00","id":894742,"title":"","content":"Or they could be made to be compatible to start with. Would it kill the developers to do that to avoid the headaches 1e dream crossover caused? I understand many of the 2e developers don't focus on crossover, but that doesn't mean they shouldn't try to use the same base system for the same thing for those that do like it, even if different creatures interact on their own end a bit differently. I mean, it's like saying that because werewolves see combat differently than vampires that it's okay if they used an entirely different system that doesn't mechanically mesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:32:22-07:00","id":894764,"title":"","content":"I think it's pretty obvious that Dreams and the Oneiros (and other astral realms) are <i>not </i>the same realms. So having an Oneiros Form for hanging out in the Oneiros and Dreamwalking rules for when characters are in Dreams are two completely separate things- whatever the terminology used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:38:12-07:00","id":894766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=894742#post894742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or they could be made to be compatible to start with. Would it kill the developers to do that to avoid the headaches 1e dream crossover caused? I understand many of the 2e developers don't focus on crossover, but that doesn't mean they shouldn't try to use the same base system for the same thing for those that do like it, even if different creatures interact on their own end a bit differently. I mean, it's like saying that because werewolves see combat differently than vampires that it's okay if they used an entirely different system that doesn't mechanically mesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny, because a lot of my problems with the old dreaming system stemmed from the fact that they copy-pasted randomly from Mage (namely, how to get into other's dreams was a conflicted mess). I'd rather have an independent system that is internally consistent, rather than having some things pulled from other splats halfhazardly or have the devs spend countless more hours trying to make every subsystem play nice together. <br /> <br /> Dream-stuff is hardly as ubiquitous as combat, and isn't something your baseline human can do, so I don't think that's a fair equivalency. It's more like, say, magical emotional compulsion: Vampire does it one way, Mage another, and Changeling will probably share some things (like Conditions), but will still work differently. Or heck, even like magic powers themselves; Gifts work differently from Embeds work differently from Contracts. They have different systems because the different systems work thematically. Changelings make agreements with scopes of reality, so they have discrete powers of different scale. Making them unscaling (like Demon) or fluid (like Mage) makes them feel different and not fit.<br /> <br /> Same deal with dreams: Changelings are infused bodily with dreams, so they enter bodily. Mages think their way in in, Beasts have a soul there, but neither have a body, so they follow Dream Form rules. Changelings have a body (and can make things get physical), so they don't. I'd assume that anyone using a Dream Form is, in fact, dreaming (it's in the name), and thus a Changeling can go to where they are. Beyond that...IDK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:38:54-07:00","id":894767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=894764#post894764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's pretty obvious that Dreams and the Oneiros (and other astral realms) are <i>not </i>the same realms. So having an Oneiros Form for hanging out in the Oneiros and Dreamwalking rules for when characters are in Dreams are two completely separate things- whatever the terminology used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you didn't read my previous post, but Mage and Beast use Dream Form rules in the astral AND in dreams; the dream travel spell says to use them, for instance. So no, it's not completely separate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:43:55-07:00","id":894769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=894766#post894766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's funny, because a lot of my problems with the old dreaming system stemmed from the fact that they copy-pasted randomly from Mage (namely, how to get into other's dreams was a conflicted mess). I'd rather have an independent system that is internally consistent, rather than having some things pulled from other splats halfhazardly or have the devs spend countless more hours trying to make every subsystem play nice together.<br /> <br /> Dream-stuff is hardly as ubiquitous as combat, and isn't something your baseline human can do, so I don't think that's a fair equivalency. It's more like, say, magical emotional compulsion: Vampire does it one way, Mage another, and Changeling will probably share some things (like Conditions), but will still work differently. Or heck, even like magic powers themselves; Gifts work differently from Embeds work differently from Contracts. They have different systems because the different systems work thematically. Changelings make agreements with scopes of reality, so they have discrete powers of different scale. Making them unscaling (like Demon) or fluid (like Mage) makes them feel different and not fit.<br /> <br /> Same deal with dreams: Changelings are infused bodily with dreams, so they enter bodily. Mages think their way in in, Beasts have a soul there, but neither have a body, so they follow Dream Form rules. Changelings have a body (and can make things get physical), so they don't. I'd assume that anyone using a Dream Form is, in fact, dreaming (it's in the name), and thus a Changeling can go to where they are. Beyond that...IDK.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's similarly a false equivalency. I'm not saying the powers should work exactly the same. The main issue I'm getting at here is that a Mage and a Changeling treat a MORTAL differently in dreams. I don't care that Changelings go there physically; that's cool and thematic, and should use a different system.<br /> <br /> However, it should be COMPATIBLE, and rely on the same base system for how a third party without a power is treated in dreams; mortals specifically. If a mage and a changeling are both in a mortal's dreams, you have a mess because they both say something different happens to the mortal when damage is filled up. And for the mortal's base stats and abilities, for that matter. THAT'S what my issue is.<br /> <br /> I'm all for a Changelings <i>specifically</i> taking real damage that gets downgraded, and Mages getting a boost in their Dream Form's statistics. But both should have the dream form rules for a mortal or other third party with no special system. Just like a werewolf's Gift and a Mage's spell should both do damage to a health track in a similar manner; the effects are different, but since both do damage, you'd expect it to work the same. It'd be weird if one said the mortal gets the 'bleeding out' condition if they take Stamina + Size levels of damage from any source, and the other used actual health rules, you know? And even weirder if Werewolf had an entirely different system for a mortal's combat stats than every other book did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 05-20-2016, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:09:23-07:00","id":894791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=894769#post894769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's similarly a false equivalency. I'm not saying the powers should work exactly the same. The main issue I'm getting at here is that a Mage and a Changeling treat a MORTAL differently in dreams. I don't care that Changelings go there physically; that's cool and thematic, and should use a different system.<br /> <br /> However, it should be COMPATIBLE, and rely on the same base system for how a third party without a power is treated in dreams; mortals specifically. If a mage and a changeling are both in a mortal's dreams, you have a mess because they both say something different happens to the mortal when damage is filled up. And for the mortal's base stats, for that matter. THAT'S what my issue is.<br /> <br /> I'm all for a Changelings <i>specifically</i> taking real damage that gets downgraded, and Mages getting a boost in their Dream Form's statistics. But both should have the dream form rules for a mortal or other third party with no special system. Just like a werewolf's Gift and a Mage's spell should both do damage to a health track in a similar manner; the effects are different, but damage is damage. It'd be weird if one said the mortal gets the 'bleeding out' condition if they take Stamina + Size levels, and the other used actual health, you know? And even weirder if Werewolf had an entirely different system for a mortal's combat stats than mage did.</div> </div> </div> </div>On one hand, yeah, it would make sense if what happened to mortals when getting dream-punched by a Mage/Beast/Changeling was the same. On the other, you do have differences in the combat subsystem like that: a Vampire's bite grants the Drained Condition, but other damage sources don't, for example. The source of the attack can cause the outcome to differ, which can get confusing when trying to use both systems, but allows thematic and mechanical freedom. It's a hassle on the crossover-ST side, but simpler on the Dev side, and the mono-splat-STs are unaffected either way. I agree that it would be nice for it to be normalized, but I can understand the decision not to, and I don't think that kind of &quot;compatibility&quot; should be required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 05-20-2016, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:18:59-07:00","id":894797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=894791#post894791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On one hand, yeah, it would make sense if what happened to mortals when getting dream-punched by a Mage/Beast/Changeling was the same. On the other, you do have differences in the combat subsystem like that: a Vampire's bite grants the Drained Condition, but other damage sources don't, for example. The source of the attack can cause the outcome to differ, which can get confusing when trying to use both systems, but allows thematic and mechanical freedom. It's a hassle on the crossover-ST side, but simpler on the Dev side, and the mono-splat-STs are unaffected either way. I agree that it would be nice for it to be normalized, but I can understand the decision not to, and I don't think that compatibility should be required.</div> </div> </div> </div>A vampire's bite doing something special is, again, a false equivalence. Both explanations of combat still rely on health, willpower, defense, the aforementioned condition/tilt systems, etc. They aren't calculated differently, but template abilities may interact with the systems differently or do their own special things to them. Vampires apply Drained, but if a Werewolf is there, does that affect the Drained condition applying? No, not at all, the two can beat up that mortal together without their different abilities causing problems on the mechanical side (past needing two books open).<br /> <br /> By contrast, with dream systems, if a Mage and a Changeling are both in a third dream, you don't even know what the mortal's stats are until you decide on one as the base, and then you need to patch up the other's rules to work with that, in effect crossing out portions of that book, which I dislike being needed to make crossover work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:53:54-07:00","id":894826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=894797#post894797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A vampire's bite doing something special is, again, a false equivalence. Both explanations of combat still rely on health, willpower, defense, the aforementioned condition/tilt systems, etc. They aren't calculated differently, but template abilities may interact with the systems differently or do their own special things to them. Vampires apply Drained, but if a Werewolf is there, does that affect the Drained condition applying? No, not at all, the two can beat up that mortal together without their different abilities causing problems on the mechanical side (past needing two books open).<br /> <br /> By contrast, with dream systems, if a Mage and a Changeling are both in a third dream, you don't even know what the mortal's stats are until you decide on one as the base, and then you need to patch up the other's rules to work with that, in effect crossing out portions of that book, which I dislike being needed to make crossover work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, combat is generally a false equivalence to dreams; the former is something any- and everyone can do, the latter isn't. Even if it were equivalent, combat isn't universally the same: Vampires cause unique Conditions, Werewolves and Demons can fast-track it in different ways, etc, etc. That's the point I was trying to make. <br /> <br /> I agree that it would be nice if the subsystems were the same. However, I don't think they have to be. It's a negative, but not a failure, you know? CofD is full of contradictory subsystems. It was worse in 1e, and there's efforts to make it better in 2e, but if a previously published subsystem doesn't work for a line, I'm fine with the devs creating new rules, particularly if it saves them time and effort. It's a decision I trust them to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T11:22:48-07:00","id":894844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=894826#post894826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, combat is generally a false equivalence to dreams; the former is something any- and everyone can do, the latter isn't. Even if it were equivalent, combat isn't universally the same: Vampires cause unique Conditions, Werewolves and Demons can fast-track it in different ways, etc, etc. That's the point I was trying to make.<br /> <br /> I agree that it would be nice if the subsystems were the same. However, I don't think they have to be. It's a negative, but not a failure, you know? CofD is full of contradictory subsystems. It was worse in 1e, and there's efforts to make it better in 2e, but if a previously published subsystem doesn't work for a line, I'm fine with the devs creating new rules, particularly if it saves them time and effort. It's a decision I trust them to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Any mortal can defend themselves in dreams in 2e, if I recall (I don't have the changeling playtest open here right now), using their base traits. Lucid dreamers can learn some dream riding techniques, but everyone in both changeling and mage/beast alike has a base form they use in dreams, and that they can defend themselves with. A mortal that isn't magical in any way still uses Dream Form traits, for instance, in mage. So you DO need a base system there.<br /> <br /> And I get your point, I just don't think it has anything to do with this; powers and abilities are different, but they're compatible in combat, simple as that. Combat's rules between lines can successfully be run without house rulings (past maybe deciding if something's supernatural enough to not let Vamps downgrade the damage). Dreams can't without patchworking a new system. That's the point I'M trying to make.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with devs creating new systems for how a splat can accomplish things, but I disagree about it being okay for them to make contradictory bases for them. Look at how simple dream form rules are at base; I don't think they saved any significant time or effort by not pressing ctrl c ctrl v in the mortal section, and then adding &quot;Changelings don't determine traits this way, because they're physically present in dreams, as described above, but damage caused by them to a mortal or other character's dream form affects dream health normally.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT; Whatever the case, I do see you're agreeing that it's at least a positive thing if they ARE compatible, don't get me wrong. I'm just trying to make it clear why I think it's a somewhat bigger deal than you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 05-20-2016, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T18:47:52-07:00","id":895208,"title":"","content":"I looked up how the Astral Plane works in 2e, and Dreams are the shallow part of the Astral Plane, their not even concidered a proper part of it and Mages don't normally need to defends themselves in it, and it even has seperate rules from how the rest of the Astral Plane works, for example not needing Demense, Hollows, or Synasi to access it.<br /> <br /> So the way I see it, the Astral Plane Proper uses the Dream Form rules, but Changelings don't have access to the Astral Planes Proper without the help of a Beast and its lair, so normally it won't come up.<br /> <br /> Now if a Mage is simple accessing normal dreams, both use Changing rules, just my opinion.<br /> <br /> What really funny is what happens when a mage uses the spell Sleep of the Just on a Changeling and finds to his surprise, the Changeling just vanished!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T19:46:52-07:00","id":895245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=895208#post895208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I looked up how the Astral Plane works in 2e, and Dreams are the shallow part of the Astral Plane, their not even concidered a proper part of it and Mages don't normally need to defends themselves in it, and it even has seperate rules from how the rest of the Astral Plane works, for example not needing Demense, Hollows, or Synasi to access it.<br /> <br /> So the way I see it, the Astral Plane Proper uses the Dream Form rules, but Changelings don't have access to the Astral Planes Proper without the help of a Beast and its lair, so normally it won't come up.<br /> <br /> Now if a Mage is simple accessing normal dreams, both use Changing rules, just my opinion.<br /> <br /> What really funny is what happens when a mage uses the spell Sleep of the Just on a Changeling and finds to his surprise, the Changeling just vanished!</div> </div> </div> </div>That might work as a house rule in a changeling game, but mage DOES specifically say you use dream form rules for dreams too:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">The mage manifests in dream form while in the Astral or her<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">own dreams. </span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Dream Reaching then says that you use the same systems for the Reach effect of ending up in someone else's dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 05-20-2016, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T02:18:54-07:00","id":895395,"title":"","content":"Crap, okay you win that one.<br /> <br /> But at least I'm right aboit Sleep of the Just having a weird effect on Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T04:31:30-07:00","id":895414,"title":"","content":"It's honestly not hard to make them compatible. Changeling differentiates three &quot;classes&quot; of Dreamer: Normal, Lucid, and Changeling(-like). Sleepers project a Dream Form. Normally, if someone's Dream Form is reduced to 0 HLs then they suffer the Soul Shocked condition. If they are a Lucid Dreamer then they suffer downgraded damage upon awakening and if they &quot;die&quot; in the dream they still suffer the Soul Shocked condition. In exchange they can use environmental attacks, half their supernatural advantage as a damage bonus, dream riding, dreamscaping (if they are somehow in someone else's dreams), dream scouring, dream bolstering, and remember their dreams perfectly. I'd also lean towards letting Lucid Dreamers take relevant dream merits.<br /> <br /> If they are physically present in the dream then they use their normal attributes, add +(Wyrd) to their Derived Traits (Health Levels, Defense, Initiative, Speed, Willpower), &quot;real&quot; damage is applied instantly and it is not downgraded. Too Solid Flesh turns everyone into a Lucid Dreamer and ensures damage is not downgraded when they are damage. Include a sidebar that says supernaturals with their own rules regarding being in dreams use their rules to determine traits instead and use a Beast's Horror as an example and decide whether they count as lucid dreamers or not. I lean no, even if it's illogical, unless they take the lucid dreamer merit. This is just because it'd make the Changeling book override other books. The 10-again thing is weirdly the most difficult thing to fit in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 05-21-2016, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T18:15:09-07:00","id":895783,"title":"","content":"For what its worth, I think changelings, mages, Bastets, and Beasts would rarely run into each other, they usually don't fuck with each others turf, except when Mages choose to be nosy, and given tje volume of secret for mages to explore, it'd be a rare one to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T15:57:45-07:00","id":925539,"title":"","content":"Rereading the oneiromancy of changelings, it seems like only they downgrade damage, where other people don't take any damage upon leaving the dream, though if you want to make them suffer from soul shock vs losing one or two will power as the changeling book states, in think that'd be fair.<br /> <br /> As per if they can enter the astral by dream riding a mage in trance or a beast, I'd say no. One beasts don't dream, so there's nothing to ride, and secondly changelings can't leave the dream layer of the astral without means outside themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T22:20:49-07:00","id":925714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=895414#post895414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's honestly not hard to make them compatible.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a lot easier to say than it is to do.<br /> <br /> I've been doing rewrites to make them compatible. It's actually a remarkably big undertaking. When the original rules were written, the Mage equivalent rules didn't exist. So, those all have to be scrapped and redone, along with any associated mechanics, and a surprising amount of setting/flavor material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T22:45:45-07:00","id":925728,"title":"","content":"I hope not too much setting/flavour material ended up scrapped in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T05:21:03-07:00","id":925832,"title":"","content":"I did a cheat sheet for a crossover game I'm in that covers both of them. I can post it later.<br /> <br /> Oh. Can I make one request for the rewrites? Would you be up for reconsidering what skills are used for Oneiromancy? It requires so many different skills that it is difficult to build &quot;an Oneiromancy expert&quot; and the emphasis on social skills makes it difficult to play the Autumn Erudite Oneiromancy archtype, which I think is what most people sit down expecting to do. Alternatively, a way to approach dreams physically / mentally / socially (maybe via merits?) Would work.<br /> <br /> Right now I made an Oneiromancer via universal Specialty (/ies) which feels awkward.<br /> <br /> Also please keep physically entering dreams and the dream / hedge connection and Oneroi being a thing. Those were really cool and made the different world's of changeling connected in a good way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T05:27:58-07:00","id":925836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=894797#post894797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A vampire's bite doing something special is, again, a false equivalence. Both explanations of combat still rely on health, willpower, defense, the aforementioned condition/tilt systems, etc. They aren't calculated differently, but template abilities may interact with the systems differently or do their own special things to them. Vampires apply Drained, but if a Werewolf is there, does that affect the Drained condition applying? No, not at all, the two can beat up that mortal together without their different abilities causing problems on the mechanical side (past needing two books open).<br /> <br /> By contrast, with dream systems, if a Mage and a Changeling are both in a third dream, you don't even know what the mortal's stats are until you decide on one as the base, and then you need to patch up the other's rules to work with that, in effect crossing out portions of that book, which I dislike being needed to make crossover work.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think the simplest solution is come up with a reason why those rules never interact. Like Changelings can't enter the Astral Realms at all, except for a Beasts lair, at which point they change from Dreamwalking to Dream Form, because they're playing in the Beasts home now, not they're own.<br /> <br /> When a Mage and Changeling are in the same dream, they never met because they're exploring it on seperate layers of reality, but any major changes to a dream both are manipulating provoke a clash of wills, even if there is no direct interaction.<br /> <br /> Mages and Horrors can't access Dream Bastions even in the Hedge, period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 07-04-2016, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T05:32:33-07:00","id":925838,"title":"","content":"Crap on a cracker I meant to qoute David Hill, not Falcon, my apologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T05:34:19-07:00","id":925839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=925714#post925714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a lot easier to say than it is to do.<br /> <br /> I've been doing rewrites to make them compatible. It's actually a remarkably big undertaking. When the original rules were written, the Mage equivalent rules didn't exist. So, those all have to be scrapped and redone, along with any associated mechanics, and a surprising amount of setting/flavor material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the simplest solution is come up with a reason why those rules never interact. Like Changelings can't enter the Astral Realms at all, except for a Beasts lair, at which point they change from Dreamwalking to Dream Form, because they're playing in the Beasts home now, not they're own.<br /> <br /> When a Mage and Changeling are in the same dream, they never met because they're exploring it on seperate layers of reality, but any major changes to a dream both are manipulating provoke a clash of wills, even if there is no direct interaction.<br /> <br /> Mages and Horrors can't access Dream Bastions even in the Hedge, period.<br /> <br /> There that's what I intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T05:48:35-07:00","id":925845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=925728#post925728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope not too much setting/flavour material ended up scrapped in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah me too, I love the dreamwalking rules, they're awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T05:55:40-07:00","id":925848,"title":"","content":"Oh and during a Mage or Beast vs. Changeling Clash of Wills over control of the dream, the losing party is expelled from the dream.<br /> <br /> Alternately when a Mage/Beast or Changeling both enter the same dream, it provokes a Clash of Wills, not of the Mage or Changeling, but of the Astral's influence on the dream vs. The Hedge's influence on the dream using the Characters stats.<br /> <br /> If the Astral wins you use the Dream form rules and if the Hedge wins you use Dreamwalking rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T12:12:14-07:00","id":926014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=925839#post925839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the sicompatibility.n is come up with a reason why those rules never interact. Like Changelings can't enter the Astral Realms at all, except for a Beasts lair, at which point they change from Dreamwalking to Dream Form, because they're playing in the Beasts home now, not they're own.<br /> <br /> When a Mage and Changeling are in the same dream, they never met because they're exploring it on seperate layers of reality, but any major changes to a dream both are manipulating provoke a clash of wills, even if there is no direct interaction.<br /> <br /> Mages and Horrors can't access Dream Bastions even in the Hedge, period.<br /> <br /> There that's what I intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad to hear rewrites are being done for compatibility.<br /> <br /> And to be perfectly blunt, omega, I think your idea would be an arbitrary prevention of fun crossover scenes and possibilities with no real gain to the game itself, and a terrible direction for design. I sincerely hope the developers do NOT go that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 07-04-2016, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T12:39:07-07:00","id":926033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=926014#post926014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">F<br /> I'm glad to hear rewrites are being done for compatibility. And to be perfectly blunt, omega, i think your idea of &quot;prevent crossover scenes and stories&quot; would be a terrible way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Falco gets it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T12:44:03-07:00","id":926034,"title":"","content":"Was on my tablet and tweaked my wording a bit now that I'm on my PC and don't have to worry about difficulties typing, but regardless, same basic idea.<br /> <br /> As to actually helpful suggestions, I think the main issue that needs to be worked through for compatibility is simply change it so non-changelings/native oneiroi simply use Dream Form rules, and tweak it a bit so that's more compatible. So, your typical dream form dreamer doesn't suffer downgraded damage, they deal with soul shock.<br /> <br /> Changelings could still physically be present in dreams and use the stats as presented without it being incompatible, you just need to make sure the base rules for everyone else account for the fact that non-changelings (/huntsmen/gentry) AREN'T physically there, so they work properly with other systems that similarly use dream forms. As I've mentioned before, the biggest deal isn't that changelings have their own dice pools, it's that they claim mortals and similar third parties have different traits than other splats say they do. It's that whole 'third party involved' thing that creates the largest issues.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T13:15:34-07:00","id":926049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=926014#post926014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad to hear rewrites are being done for compatibility.<br /> <br /> And to be perfectly blunt, omega, I think your idea would be an arbitrary prevention of fun crossover scenes and possibilities with no real gain to the game itself, and a terrible direction for design. I sincerely hope the developers do NOT go that route.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its an effient solution to a problem that appears to have become a major obstacle to finishing Changeling. <br /> <br /> How often will this come up?<br /> <br /> I don't want to lose all the cool elements of Dreamwalking, so that those rare occasions that a Changeling and a Mage/Beast meet in a dream their playing the exact same way, losing all the unique Changeling flavour.<br /> <br /> Since my simple idea appears to be unpopular, I suppose if you do want to combine Dream Form and Dreaming walking a starting point could be that Incubi are really Goetics that have been granted a body made of Glamour, Goetics effectively fused with glamour, becoming Fae, so they can interact with the Hedge, Arcadia, and Ironside.<br /> <br /> Dreamform stats could be used for Goetics, Mages, Beasts, Bastets, Fae Touched and other beings that are their mentally/spiritually there, ect..., and Dreamwalking for Changelings, Huntsmen, Succubi, Incubi, Baku, True Fae and simular beings, that are present in the dream physically.<br /> <br /> This should be no problem, its no worse then manifested spirits fighting say a werewolf, they use different types of stats.<br /> <br /> I'll review the rules and see what else I can come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T13:20:41-07:00","id":926051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=926034#post926034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's that they claim mortals and similar third parties have different traits than other splats say they do. It's that whole 'third party involved' thing that creates the largest issues.</div> </div> </div> </div> good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T13:26:14-07:00","id":926052,"title":"","content":"In an interesting twist for the Too Solid Flesh tilt would be for it to force those in Dream Form into a more physical dreamwalking form, but that might be hard to impliment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T14:45:20-07:00","id":926096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=926049#post926049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its an effient solution to a problem that appears to have become a major obstacle to finishing Changeling.<br /> <br /> How often will this come up?<br /> <br /> I don't want to lose all the cool elements of Dreamwalking, so that those rare occasions that a Changeling and a Mage/Beast meet in a dream their playing the exact same way, losing all the unique Changeling flavour.<br /> <br /> Since my simple idea appears to be unpopular, I suppose if you do want to combine Dream Form and Dreaming walking a starting point could be that Incubi are really Goetics that have been granted a body made of Glamour, Goetics effectively fused with glamour, becoming Fae, so they can interact with the Hedge, Arcadia, and Ironside.<br /> <br /> Dreamform stats could be used for Goetics, Mages, Beasts, Bastets, Fae Touched and other beings that are their mentally/spiritually there, ect..., and Dreamwalking for Changelings, Huntsmen, Succubi, Incubi, Baku, True Fae and simular beings, that are present in the dream physically.<br /> <br /> This should be no problem, its no worse then manifested spirits fighting say a werewolf, they use different types of stats.<br /> <br /> I'll review the rules and see what else I can come up with.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically what I've been suggesting. Having different stats for the splats themselves is no issue, so long as neither side claims &quot;everyone else works X way&quot; in a way that makes crossover hard to arbitrate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T10:36:20-07:00","id":926498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=926096#post926096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's basically what I've been suggesting. Having different stats for the splats themselves is no issue, so long as neither side claims &amp;quot;everyone else works X way&amp;quot; in a way that makes crossover hard to arbitrate.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh I understand that was what you were getting at, I was just explaining were I would make the divide, including having Fae Touched with the right merit use dream form rules instead of dreamwalking rules or even part of them, because a they don't physically enter the dream like Changelings, Incubi, Succubi, Baku, True Fae, Huntsmen, ect... Not just splat vs. Splat, but Mental/Spiritual form vs. Physical dreamwalking.<br /> <br /> And I think trying Goetics incubi makes sense to me, plus it plays back to the Goetic Demons of Mage 1e to my amusement (Goetic Demobs vs Incubi).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T10:46:44-07:00","id":926508,"title":"","content":"Tying Incubi to Goetics also explains why cobble thought can't simple make aninate living beings, but the Too Solid Flesh Till can.<br /> <br /> Cobblethough pulls out a empty dream figment and makes it temporarily &quot;real&quot;, but it has no substance of its own, so it has no life and if you want to make it permanant you have combine it will something physically real to turn it into a hedge spun item, in the process giving it substance.<br /> <br /> Where as the Too Solid Tilt transforms a Goetic into a Fae, clothing the purely mental/spiritual beings in a solid body of glamour, and changing the nature of the Goetic by the fusion, so it ends up a Fae Incubus.<br /> <br /> This naturally removes the Goetic from the Astral Plane, as its functioning like the Incubi's soul, and functioning as tge essence/lifeforce that animates it and makes it permenant, unlike Cobblethough objects.<br /> <br /> And most Too Solid Flesh objects, are likely just rank 0 Goetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T10:50:38-07:00","id":926511,"title":"","content":"I know Cambions eat dreams most of the time, but can they dreamwalk in their own dream, if full could they choose not to devoure local dreams?<br /> <br /> Can they dream craft dream vessels and hedgespun items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T08:31:29-07:00","id":930353,"title":"","content":"I'm really curious as to what the dreamwalking rules look like now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T09:16:08-07:00","id":930894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/892837-2e-dream-form-vs-dreamwalking?p=926511#post926511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know Cambions eat dreams most of the time, but can they dreamwalk in their own dream, if full could they choose not to devoure local dreams?<br /> <br /> Can they dream craft dream vessels and hedgespun items.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cambions don't require food, oxygen, or blood to survive either but the feed off glamour directly. In the mortal world they instinctively devour the glamour of everyone in the vicinity. Mortals around them rarely have dreams at all and any they might have are dead things that provide no glamour to the Hedge. </div> </div> </div>Cambions don't eat dreams directly, they eat glamour that people naturally produce before it can be invested into dreams. Thus people around them don't dream very much because they don't have the glamour to <i>make</i> them. They cut off the hedge's natural glamour supply at the source. I would imagine that if they get into the hedge they wouldn't enter dreams at all, they'd slurp Bastions up for dinner without ever going inside them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T13:10:16-07:00","id":930997,"title":"","content":"What about when the Cambion sleeps, do Cambions form their own dream bastions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T05:37:45-07:00","id":931288,"title":"","content":"I would say yes, but probably not the same way changelings do. There probably isn't anything preventing them from taking the Lucid Dreamer merit. But if I was running a game with them I might make their Bastions inverted - soak up glamour in the hedge while they sleep instead of releasing it into the hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T17:09:35-07:00","id":931698,"title":"","content":"Took me like forever to post this, but... I made it as a primer for oneiromancy for other players in a mixed venue game. It reconciles Changeling rules and dream form rules.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dream Form</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instead of the nine Attributes used by physical characters, characters in Dream Form use the three simplified traits of Power, Finesse, and Resistance. For human (and most supernatural) characters translating into Dream Form, these are equal to the mental traits \u2014 use Intelligence for Power, Wits for Finesse, and Resolve for Resistance. Characters retain their skills and may use them normally within the confines of the dream so long as it makes sense.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some creatures, such as Changelings, can enter dreams physically. Those who physically enter dream use their normal traits instead of dream form traits and they have deal with damage normally. As natives to the dreams, challenging them is like wading through molasses. Non-Lucid Dreamers do not gain the 10-again quality to their rolls against people who are physically present in the dream.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Derived Traits</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Dream Health</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is not linked to Size as physical Health is, but instead to the determination and the potential of the dreamer. In game terms, this is Resistance + (the dreaming character\u2019s Attribute Maximum), which for humans is five but for supernatural beings usually increases when they reach high levels of their Supernatural Tolerance Trait. The last boxes of Dream Health impose wound penalties when filled just as physical Health does. If a person would be \u201ckilled\u201d in a Dream, they instead wake up completely fine, except for the Soul Shocked condition.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Dream Defense </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">is calculated like physical defense, using the character\u2019s Power and Finesse in place of the character\u2019s Wits and Dexterity. This means for most characters their Dream Defense will be (lower of Power and Finesse) + Athletics.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Willpower </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">is unchanged. Use the character\u2019s normal willpower maximum and willpower pool in their dream form. A character may spend willpower normally while in dream form. Note that you do not regain willpower for sleeping until you wake up.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Initiative</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is equal to the character\u2019s Power + Finesse.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Speed</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is equal to the character\u2019s Species Factor + Power + Finesse, although the narrative of the dream has more of a bearing on thing's relative location.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Size</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is a narrative construct within a dream. It can be anything at any moment, and has no impact on the mechanics of the game.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other Things to Be Aware Of</span></span><ul><li><i>Bastion </i>is your first line of defense against intruders into your dreams, and is equal to your Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance.</li> <li>When your dream form attacks, it may use any combat skill appropriate to the narration. The <i>Weapon Modifier</i> for all such personal attacks is equal to half of your Supernatural Tolerance, rounded up. All attacks can deal Lethal or Bashing damage.</li> <li><i>Dream Intensity</i> is how vivid and memorable the dream is. At the beginning of a scene involving your dreams, roll Wits + Resolve. Changelings add their Wyrd to this roll.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The dreamer wakes unrested and without dreaming. She doesn't regain a point of Willpower.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The dreamer does not remember the events of her dream upon waking.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The dreamer remembers the dream upon waking, though details quickly fade and the entire dream is forgotten after a few hours unless recorded or something reminds them of it later. The Intensity of the dream may help or hinder various dreamwalking techniques.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The dream sticks with the dreamer in such detail that it is perfectly</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">remembered even years later.</span></span><ul><li>Magic works normally within the confines of a dream unless that magic is dependent on communing with an entity or a realm that doesn\u2019t exist in dreams, such spirits, ghosts, the underworld or the hisil.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Lucid Dreamer (Merit, </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u2022\u2022</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>)</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Non-Changeling</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You are a lucid dreamer, able to perfectly remember your own dreams, regardless of their intensity. In addition, you may influence your own dreams in the following ways:</span></span><ul><li>You may change the content of your dreams at will, although large changes to the narrative require a Wits + Empathy roll.</li> <li>You may Analyze the Dream, Convince the Dreamer, and Learn About the Dreamer on yourself, but you do not add your Supernatural Tolerance to the roll.</li> <li>In Dream Combat you may utilize Environmental Attacks using your Manipulation + Expression + Supernatural Tolerance - Target\u2019s Defense, using half of your Supernatural Tolerance (rounded up) as your weapon modifier.</li> <li>You may wake up with a Wits + Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance - Dream\u2019s Bastion rating roll.</li> <li>You use the 10-again quality when rolling against things that are physically present in dreams.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Your dreams are far too real sometimes. When you awaken, any damage to your Dream Health is downgraded (Aggravated becomes Lethal, Lethal becomes Bashing, and Bashing is ignored) and applied to your actual health.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Analyze the Dream</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By carefully observing the dream a changeling determines whether a dream is specific type or if anything not native to the dream is present. Make an Intelligence + Occult + Intensity roll. Prophetic dreams are particularly delicate and even subtle changes that don\u2019t require a roll disrupt the Wyrd\u2019s influence on the dream enough to turn it into a regular dream. With an exceptional success a changeling locates any non-natives within the dreamscape. Careful changelings will always analyze the dream before making any changes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Convince the Dreamer</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is possible to plant subliminal messages in a dreamer\u2019s mind. Roll Wits + Socialize + Wyrd - Intensity, with each roll requiring a full night\u2019s work of carefully adjusting the dream. Each roll applies to a specifically declared goal under the Social Maneuvering system (pg. XX) and a success allows the changeling to open a door or add a door to the dreamer\u2019s resistance.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Learn about the Dreamer</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dreams provide an unrestrained look into a dreamer\u2019s soul and changeling may learn quite a bit simply by observing and interpreting what they see. As long as no changes are made to the narrative of the dream, a Wits + Empathy + Wyrd + Intensity roll may be made each night. With a success, the changeling learns enough to improve their first impression two steps up on the Social Maneuvering impression chart. Achieving an exceptional success also reveals the dreamer\u2019s aspirations, virtue, vice, Clarity, a Condition they\u2019re suffering, or if any magic has influenced their mind in the past month.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Soul Shocked (Condition)</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Per the books.<br /> <br /> <i>Too Solid Flesh (Environmental Tilt)</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dreams are all too real and what happens while in the dream happens physically as well.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect: All participants in the dream gain the benefits of Lucid Dreaming and will clearly remember what occurs regardless of the dream\u2019s total Intensity. Damage is not downgraded upon transitioning from the dream to the waking world. Pieces of the dream can survive the usual dissolution into glamour, and escape into the Hedge as physical objects or hobgoblins known as Oneiroi when the dream ends.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Causing the Tilt:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A changeling rolls an exceptional success when bolstering the Intensity of a dream.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ending the Tilt:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Tilt ends when the dream ends and the dreamer wakes or dies.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 07-14-2016, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T00:45:28-07:00","id":931880,"title":"","content":"Looks pretty good so far, but I think in some places needs additional notes for other character types. For instance, I think characters using dream altering powers should count as 'lucid dreamers' for the purpose of dream combat and 10-again, and some supernaturals should probably add ST to their Intensity similarly to changelings, similar to 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}